 {"id": "AUG-055", "title": "answer accepts a --chosen that matches no --option: a success line over a configuration that selects NOTHING", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "status": "complete", "reasoning": "WHY (found live 2026-09-24, 5th dogfood run, namespace df5-real)\n\nThe single most damaging defect a user hits, because it is silent and it defeats\nthe loop's last step.\n\n`answer` inserts its option rows with `active = (opt == a.chosen)` \u2014 a VERBATIM\nSTRING EQUALITY between the --chosen text and the --option text (auger.py\ncmd_answer, the option insert). Nothing validates the pair, nothing warns, and\nthe pair is easy to miss because `--option` is naturally a full sentence while\n--chosen is naturally a short name for it.\n\nReproduced verbatim:\n  answer --question-id Q-000001 --chosen \"The CI box smoke test\" \\\n         --option \"CI smoke battery: bunker3 runs the project's own documented\n                   smoke check ...\" --why-not \"...\"\n  -> D-001 recorded  (confidence -1.0, 1 options, embedded, scope project)\n     closed Q-000001\n  dump\n  -> ACTIVE CONFIGURATION: (nothing active)\n     WARNING: decisions with != 1 active option:\n       - D-001: 0 of 1 options active \u2014 this decision contributes NOTHING\n\nEvery subsequent verb inherits the damage: `dump --config` then compares the\nhypothesis against a record whose chosen text is not any option, so it reports a\nspurious CONTRADICTION (\"choosing <option label> contradicts the recorded choice\n(<the different sentence>)\") for a hypothesis that actually agrees with it.\n\nThe documentation invites this: docs/VERBS.md says `--option` is \"repeatable \u2014\nevery alternative, chosen ones included\" and `--chosen` is \"the choice\", with no\nstatement that the two must be byte-identical.\n\nDELIVERABLE (pick one, but the first two are the fix)\n- validate that --chosen resolves to exactly one of the supplied --option values\n  before anything is stored, refusing by name otherwise (the resolve_option\n  machinery already exists and already refuses loudly); OR\n- make --chosen accept an option token (D-001-O3 / O3 / a label) and derive the\n  chosen label from the option row, so the two can never disagree; AND\n- whatever the mechanism, the success line must state the resulting active-option\n  count (\"D-001 recorded (1 of 3 options active)\"), so an empty configuration can\n  never be printed as a clean success.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- `answer --chosen <text not among --option>` exits non-zero naming the mismatch,\n  OR is accepted with the chosen option auto-activated \u2014 and in either case stores\n  exactly one active option\n- the recorded decision renders in `dump` with exactly one active option and NO\n  spurious contradiction line in `dump --config` for a hypothesis that matches it\n- the success line reports the active-option count\n- a regression test covers the mismatched-wording case (chosen a sentence, option\n  a longer sentence, real use)\n- ruff check auger.py clean", "capability_tags": ["+engine", "+decision"], "attempts": 0, "blocks": [], "depends_on": [], "detail": {}, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": "Worker gpt-5.6-luna@openai-codex commit 391f0ea. Foreman verified py_compile, ruff, and 3 focused regressions. GitReins Tier 1 PASS and Tier 2 COMPLETE/PASS (verdict 51e9a232, directory b91e81e5): 139 pytest, smoke 21/21, LIVE ARMS 2/0 skipped, GATE PASS. GitHub CI success. origin/main parity 0.", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "commit_hash": "391f0eaccb9f7f8952abeab511707e3b1150d3bc", "perpetual": null, "created_at": "2026-09-24T03:55:24.297805+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T07:22:25.816556+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "worker_summary": "Resolved --chosen before writes; mismatches refuse atomically; token choices canonicalize to one active option; success reports active count; docs and regressions landed.", "completed_at": "2026-09-24T07:22:25Z"}
-{"id": "AUG-056", "title": "ask re-proposes the question it just closed: the already-answered gate does not see a closed question and wastes a full round", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "status": "pending", "reasoning": "WHY (found live 2026-09-24, 5th dogfood run, namespace df5-real)\n\n`ask` proposed the IDENTICAL question text in the round immediately after the\nuser answered exactly that question.\n\nObserved sequence:\n  ask                                  -> stored Q-000001  What test proves this works?\n  answer --question-id Q-000001 ...    -> D-001 recorded, closed Q-000001\n  ask                                  -> already answered? 0.3 -> genuinely new\n                                          stored Q-000002  What test proves this works?\n  answer --question-id Q-000002 ...    -> D-002 recorded  (a DUPLICATE decision)\n  ask                                  -> question not stored: JEV proposed none:\n                                          nothing left worth asking\n\nSo the drill burned one ask (5.0s + a model call), one answer, and one duplicate\ndecision to close a question the previous answer had already closed. The loop\nself-heals only AFTER the waste.\n\nRoot cause is in the gate, not in JEV: the already-answered check scores the\nproposed question text against embedded evidence, and the evidence for D-001 was\nwritten with a chosen sentence that differs from the option label \u2014 so the noul\nscore came back 0.24-0.30 against a threshold above it. Note this is COMPOUNDED\nby AUG-055 (a mismatched --chosen also degrades the evidence text the gate reads),\nbut is not caused by it: the gate has no signal for \"the question this text came\nfrom was closed one round ago\" even when the evidence is clean.\n\nDELIVERABLE\n- carry the closed-question identity: when `answer --question-id Q` closes Q, the\n  gate must exclude Q (and the proposal text it carried) from the next round's\n  askable set \u2014 for at least one round \u2014 rather than relying on a similarity score\n  over evidence prose\n- OR record the closed question id on the decision's evidence entry and have the\n  already-answered pass treat an exact closed-question-text match as answered\n  regardless of the noul score\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- the documented loop (ask -> answer -> ask) never re-proposes the question text\n  that the previous answer closed, on a fresh namespace, reproduced as a test\n- a duplicate decision is NOT created to close a re-proposed twin\n- the second ask still works normally when the closed question was a DIFFERENT\n  text (the gate must not simply suppress the next question)\n- ruff check auger.py clean", "capability_tags": ["+engine", "+method"], "attempts": 0, "blocks": [], "depends_on": [], "detail": {}, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "perpetual": null, "created_at": "2026-09-24T03:55:24.297805+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T03:55:24.297805+00:00"}
